}
title Submission status (submissions.status)
[*] --> submitted : submissionService.create()\n(column default)
[*] --> ready_for_review : ensureReportSubmission()\n(artifact from a report)
submitted --> ready_for_review : processAiPreReview()\ncompleted
submitted --> under_review : review request created /\nexternal invitation accepted
ready_for_review --> under_review : reviewRequestService.create()
revised --> under_review : create() /\nacceptExternalInvitation()
under_review --> revision_requested : refreshSubmissionReviewStatus()
under_review --> completed : refreshSubmissionReviewStatus()
under_review --> ready_for_review : refresh after decline,\ncancel, expiry
revision_requested --> revised : createVersion(),\naddRevision()
completed --> revised : new revision or no review\nof current revision
ready_for_review --> revised : createVersion(),\naddRevision()
under_review --> revised : createVersion(),\naddRevision()
revised --> under_review : resubmit()\nwith active request
state accepted #F5F5F5
state rejected #F5F5F5
state withdrawn #F5F5F5
note right of accepted
  <b>Dead values</b>: accepted, rejected and withdrawn are only
  checked as closed states (read-only guards). No service
  function sets them. Derived statuses come from
  submissionReviewStatus() in academic-review.rules.ts.
end note
@enduml
